## 7. Luhn check-digit computation

`Owner.java` lines 607-631:
```java
public static int luhnCheckDigit(String value) {
    int sum = 0;
    boolean doubling = true;
    for (int i = (value == null ? 0 : value.length()) - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = value.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') {
            continue;
        }
        int digit = c - '0';
        if (doubling) {
            digit *= 2;
            if (digit > 9) {
                digit -= 9;
            }
        }
        sum += digit;
        doubling = !doubling;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```
Note: scans right-to-left starting with `doubling = true` (doubles the last digit). Non-digits skipped; null/digit-free yields 0. Used by `getCheckDigit()`.

